sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Student (Mobile / Web)
    participant CL as Client app (face-api.js)
    participant GW as Kong :8080
    participant ID as ms-identity :8081
    participant AZ as ms-authorization :8082
    participant BIO as ms-biometric :8086
    participant M as MongoDB faceattend_biometric
    participant ATT as ms-attendance :8085
    participant PG as PostgreSQL schema attendance
    participant K as Kafka topic attendance-events

    Note over GW: Kong's global pre-function validates the opaque sessionId against identity on every non-public route (401/503 at the edge), plus cors + rate-limiting — no jwt plugin. ms-biometric (06) also re-validates on its own: every /api/v1/biometric/facial/* route requires session + permission attendance.record:write (see SEQ-02)

    rect rgb(238, 245, 238)
    Note over CL,M: 1. Enrollment (once per student)
    S->>CL: open "register face" screen
    CL->>CL: face-api.js detects the face and computes the descriptor locally
    CL->>GW: POST /api/v1/biometric/facial/enroll {person_id, encoding}
    GW->>ID: edge pre-function: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>GW: 200 Active
    GW->>BIO: forward
    BIO->>ID: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId} (its own guard re-validates)
    ID-->>BIO: Active
    BIO->>AZ: GET /api/v1/auth/evaluate?permission=attendance.record:write
    AZ-->>BIO: allowed
    BIO->>M: upsert active template and deactivate the previous one
    M-->>BIO: ok
    BIO-->>CL: 201 Created
    end

    rect rgb(240, 245, 255)
    Note over CL,M: 2. Identify 1:N — read-only precondition, outside the write transaction (ADR-004)
    S->>CL: press "take attendance"
    CL->>CL: compute the descriptor locally (the photo is never uploaded)
    CL->>GW: POST /api/v1/biometric/facial/identify {encoding}
    GW->>ID: edge pre-function: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>GW: 200 Active
    GW->>BIO: forward
    BIO->>ID: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId} + GET /auth/evaluate (same guard as enroll)
    ID-->>BIO: Active, allowed
    BIO->>M: list active templates (cap identify_scan_limit = 10000)
    M-->>BIO: templates
    BIO->>BIO: cosine similarity of every template against the capture
    BIO->>M: insert biometric_match_logs (threshold 0.85, retention 90 days)
    alt best score >= threshold
        BIO-->>CL: 200 {person_id, score}
    else below threshold
        BIO-->>CL: 404 NO_MATCH
        CL-->>S: face not recognized — retry (nothing is written)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 246, 236)
    Note over GW,PG: 3. Attendance write — one local ACID transaction (ADR-004)
    CL->>GW: POST /api/v1/attendance-records {class_session_id, academic_actor_id, attendance_status, capture_method, match_score}
    GW->>ID: edge pre-function: GET /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}
    ID-->>GW: 200 Active
    GW->>ATT: forward with Authorization Bearer sessionId
    ATT->>ID: AuthTokenFilter re-validates: GET /sessions/{id} + GET /users/{id}/roles + evaluate
    ID-->>ATT: Active session, roles, allowed (see SEQ-02)
    ATT->>ATT: @Transactional begins
    ATT->>ATT: pre-check findByClassSessionIdAndAcademicActorId
    ATT->>PG: INSERT attendance_record
    Note over ATT,K: publish() runs inside @Transactional right after save: kafkaTemplate.send is async and failures are only logged — no outbox, no DLQ (AT-006)
    ATT->>K: send attendance-events {attendanceRecordId, status}
    PG-->>ATT: commit — uq_attendance_session_actor makes this atomic
    alt row already exists for that session and actor
        PG-->>ATT: unique violation
        ATT-->>CL: 409 DuplicateEntityException
    else new row
        ATT-->>CL: 201 Created
    end
    end

    Note over CL: Verified 2026-10: endpoints.js declares facialIdentify and AttendanceService.create has no call site — the backend is ready but neither client wires capture to the attendance write yet
    Note over K: No Kafka consumer exists anywhere in the back-end (producers only) — attendance-events is published but not consumed — no service raises notification.alert automatically (alerts are only created via ms-notification POST /api/v1/alerts)
    Note over ATT: ADR-004 describes an in-process event bus — the implemented mechanism is the Kafka topic attendance-events
